/* ==========================================================================
   network-lines.js
   Purpose: The subdued background railway network shown behind the
   selected route in the journey map preview.

   PROVENANCE:
   These are NOT paths extracted from the anonymous Wikimedia SVG (which
   was confirmed to have zero machine-readable railway-line structure - see
   earlier project inspection notes). Instead, every line here is a real,
   simplified recorded train route from the same verified CC0 dataset used
   by stations.js/routes.js: github.com/anandology/railways (trains.json).

   This is a systematic sample (every 6th train of 5202 total,
   867 lines) rather than the complete set, kept small enough to
   render as a lightweight SVG background layer. Each line is aggressively
   simplified via Douglas-Peucker (shape-preserving point reduction, not
   invented geometry) since these are for ambient visual density only -
   not for identifying any specific journey.

   Coordinates are raw [longitude, latitude] pairs, exactly like routes.js -
   conversion to on-screen coordinates happens via the same geoToMap()
   function in route-preview.js, so this file never needs to change if the
   map calibration is later refined.
   ========================================================================== */

